Z||000002||Bill Bailey||12-08-2000||05:48 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ronnie:<BR><B>How much does a GT rear clip cost? A buddy of mine wants to know how much it would cost to convert a coupe over to a GT.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ronnie If you have just a plain coupe like a 2m4 you will need more then a rear clip to make a GT, You will need GT taillights, another deck lid with or without wing you will need all the ground effect for the rear, front and back you will need all the round type moulding, also the GT wheels, also most likley a new paint job, Just change one over will never do it again. I can buy a nice runing GT cheaper. If you have a SE or a 85GT with all the ground effect you still need the clip deck lid and taillights and all the round trim. Find some one that has a GT that does not run get the whole car. I purchase a GT on E-bay about 2 wks <BR>ago with good  V-6 engine 5sp good GT body and wheels. The interior is messed no dash I will sell the complete car for 550.00 before I start taking it apart to sell. If I can be of help let me know. You are not to far from me, Bill Bailey, Deland, Fla. rbailey@n-jcenter.com<P>||||reg||1
